  "history": {
    "origins": "This unusual poker variant was contributed by Michael Sanderson. Exact origin is unclear but it likely originated in the Northeastern USA; it was certainly played at Brandeis University (Massachusetts) and now has a following in the Maryland-Virginia area and Annapolis, where it is standard fare at several poker games. The name Napalm is of unknown origin.",
    "originCountries": ["USA"],
    "timeline": [
      "1970s–1980s: Played at Brandeis University (Massachusetts); reported as Whipsaw (1979); spread to Maryland–Virginia and Annapolis area."
